# sdd-solo — roles of the agent team (7.2). Syntax is key=value like .sdd/config; lists are space separated.
# This is the repo's POLICY: which roles exist, where each may write, where each may not. Edit freely;
# init --update never overwrites a file you have changed.
# Solo project: leave it alone — with no role marker set, nothing happens.
#
# The KEYS below stay in Vietnamese on purpose: they are configuration identifiers read by a bare-bash
# githook, not prose. Renaming them would force every running repo to edit its own config file for no
# measurable gain. Role NAMES (`.ten`) are data — write them in whatever language the team speaks.
#
# Write area: a path (no * = that folder and everything under it), * inside one segment, ** any depth.
# @code_paths @test_paths @uc_test_dir @tool_paths expand from .sdd/config — never copy a path twice.
# A deny WINS over an allow. The blocking message says "this belongs to role X" (role.sh looks it up
# with role_of_path).
#
# vai_bat_buoc: khong (default — the hook only WARNS when a commit touches outside the area)
#               · nhanh-vai (blocks once a role can be inferred)
#               · moi (blocks even when no role can be inferred).
# Turn it on after `role.sh --kiem-lich-su` reports a number you are willing to accept.
vai_bat_buoc=khong
vai=A B R D T

# A · coordinator — hands out work, commits logs for roles that do not commit, asks the owner on L3.
# Writes no spec and no code.
A.ten=coordinator
A.ghi=STATE.md specs/decisions.md notes/** .sdd/**
A.cam=@code_paths @test_paths specs/vision.md
A.nhanh=
A.commit=co
A.kiem=

# B · spec — applies the wording of tickets that already have an answer. Keeps the MAIN CHECKOUT on main:
# what B writes is shared truth, and from a separate worktree C/R/D/T would read a stale main until the
# merge (the real case where D chose against a decision R had already made). Does not write
# decisions/vision/STATE.
B.ten=spec
B.ghi=specs/** notes/hoi-dap/**
B.cam=specs/decisions.md specs/vision.md STATE.md @code_paths @test_paths
B.nhanh=
B.commit=co
B.kiem=gate-check.sh --pre UC-### · layer-check.sh when editing root/core

# R · arbiter — writes only the **Answer (R):** box of a ticket, and does NOT commit (A commits).
R.ten=arbiter
R.ghi=notes/hoi-dap/**
R.cam=specs/** @code_paths @test_paths STATE.md
R.nhanh=
R.commit=khong
R.kiem=

# D · code — own worktree, branch code/uc-###. The gate's tests (uc_test_dir) belong to T: when D needs a
# different fake → a TEST-# entry in hoi-D.md.
D.ten=code
D.ghi=@code_paths @test_paths notes/hoi-dap/hoi-D.md
D.cam=@uc_test_dir specs/** STATE.md
D.nhanh=code/*
D.commit=co
D.kiem=the repo's test command — prints how many cases pass/fail

# T · test — own worktree, branch test/uc-###. Does not read D's code: table names and signatures come
# from design.md.
T.ten=test
T.ghi=@uc_test_dir notes/hoi-dap/hoi-T.md
T.cam=@code_paths specs/** STATE.md
T.nhanh=test/*
T.commit=co
T.kiem=the repo's test command — the test must be RED before any code exists
